    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Picture this: You wake up in the morning, and find your arms covered with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "布满"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " red mosquito"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "蚊子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bites",
            "ref": "v-bite"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But your dad says he doesn’t have any himself."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do mosquitoes "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "prefer",
            "ref": "v-prefer"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to bite some people over others? The answer is YES! Only female mosquitoes bite people. They need your blood to feed their eggs. Why do they prefer to bite "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "certain",
            "zh": "某些"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people more than others?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The answer "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "lies in",
            "zh": "就在……之中"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " our body "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "odour",
            "zh": "体味"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Everyone is "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "unique",
            "zh": "独特的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Female mosquitoes know what kind of blood they need. They can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sense",
            "ref": "v-sense"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " our body odour from 30 metres away."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are also many other "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "factors",
            "zh": "因素"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", like blood type"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "血型"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and carbon dioxide"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "二氧化碳"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Mosquitoes prefer to bite people with blood Type O twice as much as those with Type A."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Mosquitoes can sense carbon dioxide up to 50 metres away. When you breathe carbon dioxide out through your nose or mouth, mosquitoes will find you. That’s why you can hear them "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "buzzing",
            "ref": "v-buzz"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " around your head all night long."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
